          <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">Delete an L3/L4 firewall rule by rule_id from getScrubIpDetails Removes a previously created L3/L4 firewall rule from the Scrub IP service. The rule_id must come from the &#x60;filter_firewall.rules[].id&#x60; array returned by getScrubIpDetails — the endpoint validates the id belongs to this service before deleting. Path param: &#x60;id&#x60; (integer, required) — Scrub IP service ID. Body (JSON): {&#x60;rule_id&#x60;: integer, required}. Returns {success: true, text: &#39;Firewall Rule has been deleted.&#39;}. Errors: 400 Invalid Service, &#39;rule_id is required.&#39; or &#39;Invalid rule id&#39; (rule does not belong to this service); 401 unauthenticated; 500 if upstream Scrub::firewallDelete fails. Caveat: if the rule was the only protection against a specific source, deleting it re-exposes the IP. Siblings: createRule, scrubIpsDeleteGeoRule, deleteFilter, getScrubIpDetails.</stringProp>
        </HTTPSamplerProxy>
        <hashTree>
          <CSVDataSet guiclass="TestBeanGUI" testclass="CSVDataSet" testname="Load CSV Test Data - scrubIpsDeleteRule" enabled="true">
